! MCP INITIALIZATION, printed p.76 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.83) --
! A PRINT SUB - ROUTINE THAT WILL PRINT ASSIGNMENTS.
!
! THIRTY-SEVEN lines, of which thirty compile and SEVEN print any
! machine code at all.  It is a data page: the message buffers the
! assignment printer fills in, three hexadecimal constants, five SYN
! cards, four one-bit flags and three index words.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> FOUR OF ITS LABELS WERE ALREADY STAND-INS, AND ALL FOUR AGREE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   T BUFB1  004432.00   line 11
!   T MESSY  004451.00   line 24   printed p.74 line 55's LVI
!   T SBHDI  004455.01   line 32
!   YSCRBT   004455.03   line 34   printed p.75 line 37's BBZ -- and
!                                  the stand-in gives the BIT, 03
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE COUNTING IS THE CHECK, AND IT CHECKS SEVENTEEN TIMES <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LISTING PRINTS NO BINARY FOR CHARACTER DATA -- as it prints
! none for printed p.41's (AX) masks or pp.9-12's (IQS*) messages --
! so no character code is checked or can be.  WHAT IS CHECKED IS THE
! COUNTING, and on a page that is almost all character data the
! counting is the whole page: SEVENTEEN labels, each landing on its
! printed location, and ONE wrong character anywhere shifts every
! label after it.  All seventeen landed on the first assembly.
!
! AND THE ADVANCE IS THE DATUM'S CHARACTER COUNT, NOT THE DECLARED
! ITEM LENGTH.  Line 16 is "(IQS*)DD(BU,36,8), UNIT *" -- six
! characters -- and advances FORTY-EIGHT bits, from 004440.40 to
! 004441.20.  Thirty-six is in the card and does not drive the
! counter.  Line 14 declares 64 and advances 96 for twelve
! characters; line 15 declares 24 and advances 24 for three.
!
! THE ONE THING THE PAGE CANNOT CHECK is where a datum's blanks
! sit.  A total of forty with a thirty-four character core leaves
! six blanks, and the locations cannot say how they split.  Those
! were MEASURED at 1800 dpi against the character pitch: line 9 is
! two leading and four trailing (the "-" lands three advances after
! the comma, and the terminator five advances after the last "-"),
! line 20 has NO leading blank ("SCRATCH" starts against the comma)
! and line 21 has one.  Recorded as measurement, not as proof.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> A HEX LITERAL IS THE ONE FIELD WHERE THE C/ZERO RULE HAS NO
! >>> INTERNAL ANSWER -- AND THE COMPILED OCTAL IS THE AUTHORITY <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! listing_typography.md 13e turns on octal having no C.  A
! HEXADECIMAL literal does, so the field cannot rule it out, and
! this page has three of them.  Line 11 prints
!
!     DD(BU),(16)C C 0 F 9 D B 6 8 B C D 9 1 9 1
!
! with THREE open-C shapes and ONE closed zero among its four zeros.
! Its compiled datum prints 0000174733321303310621, which is
! 000F9DB68B0D9191 -- so all four are zeros and the open shapes are
! the artifact.  NOTHING IN THE STATEMENT COULD HAVE SAID SO.
!
! Line 19 is sharper still: "(16)8993151193000000" prints its six
! trailing zeros as C 0 C 0 C 0, ALTERNATING, and its compiled datum
! 1046230521062300000000 = 8993151193000000 proves all six are
! zeros.  printed p.74 line 10's "CM0000" prints C M O C O C -- the
! same alternation in the opposite phase.  THE SHAPE ALTERNATES WITH
! THE COLUMN, NOT WITH THE DIGIT, which is why a run of identical
! zeros comes out in two shapes and why no "it looked like a C"
! reading of a single glyph is worth anything on its own.
!
! Line 18 was misread a THIRD way: its sixth hex digit was read 0
! and is D.  The compiled octal said so before the 1800 dpi render
! confirmed it.
!
! TWO LISTING MARKS: lines 10 and 21.

        SLC, (8)4423.40

        CNOP                         ! line 8
TBUF01  (IQS*)DD(BU,64,8),  --- SET UP THE FOLLOWING UNITS ---    *
TMBLK   (IQS*)DD(BU,64,8),        *
TBUFB1  DD(BU),(16)000F9DB68B0D9191
        (IQS*)DD(BU), MOUNT - REEL NUMBER *
TREELX  (IQS*)DD(BU,64,8),        *
        (IQS*)DD(BU,64,8), ON CHANNEL *
TCHANX  (IQS*)DD(BU,24,8),   *
        (IQS*)DD(BU,36,8), UNIT *
TUNITX  (IQS*)DD(BU),      *
        DD(BU),(16)00171D8315008B8F
        DD(BU),(16)8993151193000000
TSCRAT  (IQS*)DD(BU,64,8),SCRATCH *
TSUBHD  (IQS*)DD(BU,8,8), -- PROBLEM PROGRAM --- *
TPID    (IQS*)DD(BU,64,8),        *
        CNOP                         ! line 23
TMESSY  (A*)DD(BU), I/O REQ. INCOMP WITH MACH CONF.*
TXA     SYN, $2
TXB     SYN, $3
TXC     SYN, $4
TIXZ    SYN, $5
TIXY    SYN, $6
THEAD   DD(BU,1), 0
TSBHDI  DD(BU,1), 0
TNGATE  DD(BU,1), 0
YSCRBT  DD(BU,1), (2)0
TP5IN   XW
TP5OUT  XW
TPSAV   XW
        END, TBUF01

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKED ROWS -- all seven that print machine code.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  8  004423.40  000000.30 00                   CNOP
!   line 11  004432.00  0000174733321303310621         T BUFB1  DD(BU),(16)000F9DB68B0D9191
!   line 18  004442.00  0000270730142500105617         DD(BU),(16)00171D8315008B8F
!   line 19  004443.00  1046230521062300000000         DD(BU),(16)8993151193000000
!   line 35  004456.00  000000.00+ 000 000000 000000   T P5IN  XW
!   line 36  004457.00  000000.00+ 000 000000 000000   T P5OUT  XW
!   line 37  004460.00  000000.00+ 000 000000 000000   T PSAV  XW
